{
  "notes": "<h3>Standard integrals</h3><table><tr><td>$\\int x^n dx = \\dfrac{x^{n+1}}{n+1}$</td><td>$\\int \\dfrac{dx}{x} = \\ln|x|$</td><td>$\\int e^x dx = e^x$</td><td>$\\int a^x dx = \\dfrac{a^x}{\\ln a}$</td></tr><tr><td>$\\int \\tan x\\,dx = \\ln|\\sec x|$</td><td>$\\int \\cot x\\,dx = \\ln|\\sin x|$</td><td>$\\int \\sec x\\,dx = \\ln|\\sec x + \\tan x|$</td><td>$\\int \\text{cosec}\\,x\\,dx = \\ln|\\text{cosec}\\,x - \\cot x|$</td></tr><tr><td>$\\int \\dfrac{dx}{x^2 + a^2} = \\dfrac1a\\tan^{-1}\\dfrac xa$</td><td>$\\int \\dfrac{dx}{x^2 - a^2} = \\dfrac1{2a}\\ln\\left|\\dfrac{x-a}{x+a}\\right|$</td><td>$\\int \\dfrac{dx}{a^2 - x^2} = \\dfrac1{2a}\\ln\\left|\\dfrac{a+x}{a-x}\\right|$</td><td>$\\int \\dfrac{dx}{\\sqrt{a^2 - x^2}} = \\sin^{-1}\\dfrac xa$</td></tr><tr><td>$\\int \\dfrac{dx}{\\sqrt{x^2 \\pm a^2}} = \\ln|x + \\sqrt{x^2 \\pm a^2}|$</td><td>$\\int \\sqrt{a^2 - x^2}\\,dx = \\dfrac x2\\sqrt{a^2-x^2} + \\dfrac{a^2}{2}\\sin^{-1}\\dfrac xa$</td><td colspan=2>$\\int e^x[f(x) + f'(x)]dx = e^x f(x)$</td></tr></table><h3>Methods</h3><ul><li>Substitution; $\\int \\dfrac{f'(x)}{f(x)}dx = \\ln|f(x)|$.</li><li>By parts (ILATE order for $u$): $\\int uv\\,dx = u\\int v - \\int u'\\left(\\int v\\right)$. $\\int x e^x dx = (x-1)e^x$, $\\int \\ln x\\,dx = x\\ln x - x$.</li><li>Partial fractions for rational functions; complete the square for quadratics.</li></ul><h3>Definite integral properties</h3><ul><li>$\\int_a^b f(x)dx = \\int_a^b f(a + b - x)dx$; in particular $\\int_0^a f(x)dx = \\int_0^a f(a-x)dx$ (King's rule — use for $\\int_0^{\\pi/2}\\dfrac{\\sqrt{\\sin x}}{\\sqrt{\\sin x}+\\sqrt{\\cos x}}dx = \\dfrac\\pi4$).</li><li>$\\int_{-a}^a f(x)dx = 2\\int_0^a f(x)dx$ if $f$ even; $= 0$ if $f$ odd.</li><li>$\\int_0^{2a} f(x)dx = 2\\int_0^a f(x)dx$ if $f(2a-x) = f(x)$; $= 0$ if $f(2a-x) = -f(x)$.</li><li>$\\int_0^{\\pi/2}\\ln\\sin x\\,dx = -\\dfrac\\pi2\\ln2$; $\\int_0^{\\pi/2}\\sin^2x\\,dx = \\int_0^{\\pi/2}\\cos^2x\\,dx = \\dfrac\\pi4$; $\\int_0^{\\pi/2}\\dfrac{\\sin^n x}{\\sin^n x + \\cos^n x}dx = \\dfrac\\pi4$.</li></ul><h3>Exam tip</h3><p>The single highest-weightage maths chapter (4–5 questions). At least two are on definite-integral properties (odd/even, King's rule); one on a standard form; one on by-parts or $e^x[f + f']$.</p>",
